concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-10a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "10A APS Employment Principles"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-10a ;
    values:originalText "APS Employment Principles (1) The APS is a career-based public service that: (a) makes fair employment decisions with a fair system of review; and (b) recognises that the usual basis for engagement is as an ongoing APS employee; and (c) makes decisions relating to engagement and promotion that are based on merit; and (d) requires effective performance from each employee; and (e) provides flexible, safe and rewarding workplaces where communication, consultation, cooperation and input from employees on matters that affect their workplaces are valued; and (f) provides workplaces that are free from discrimination, patronage and favouritism; and (g) recognises the diversity of the Australian community and fosters diversity in the workplace. Decisions based on merit (2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(c), a decision relating to engagement or promotion is based on merit if: (a) all eligible members of the community were given a reasonable opportunity to apply to perform the relevant duties; and (b) an assessment is made of the relative suitability of the candidates to perform the relevant duties, using a competitive selection process; and" ;
    skos:definition "APS Employment Principles (1) The APS is a career-based public service that: (a) makes fair employment decisions with a fair system of review; and (b) recognises that the usual basis for engagement is as an ongoing APS employee; and (c) makes decisions relating to engagement and promotion that are based on merit; and (d) requires effective performance from each employee; and (e) provides flexible, safe and rewarding workplaces where communication, consultation, cooperation and input from employees on matters that affect their workplaces are valued; and (f) provides workplaces that are free from discrimination, patronage and favouritism; and (g) recognises the diversity of the Australian community and fosters diversity in the workplace. Decisions based on merit (2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(c), a decision relating to engagement or promotion is based on merit if: (a) all eligible members of the community were given a reasonable opportunity to apply to perform the relevant duties; and (b) an assessment is made of the relative suitability of the candidates to perform the relevant duties, using a competitive selection process; and"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "4920f0cab8b746ff9a5d8f8fae9b35805465a74c1b04cf61b0ce0bce13cab46d" ;
    cof:pageNumber "15"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-10a-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-10a-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <public-service-act-1999.pdf> ;
    dc:source "public-service-act-1999.pdf, p.15" .
doc:sec-10a a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "10A APS Employment Principles" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "APS Employment Principles (1) The APS is a career-based public service that: (a) makes fair employment decisions with a fair system of review; and (b) recognises that the usual basis for engagement is as an ongoing APS employee; and (c) makes decisions relating to engagement and promotion that are based on merit; and (d) requires effective performance from each employee; and (e) provides flexible, safe and rewarding workplaces where communication, consultation, cooperation and input from employees on matters that affect their workplaces are valued; and (f) provides workplaces that are free from discrimination, patronage and favouritism; and (g) recognises the diversity of the Australian community and fosters diversity in the workplace. Decisions based on merit (2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(c), a decision relating to engagement or promotion is based on merit if: (a) all eligible members of the community were given a reasonable opportunity to apply to perform the relevant duties; and (b) an assessment is made of the relative suitability of the candidates to perform the relevant duties, using a competitive selection process; and" ;
    cof:pageNumber "15"^^xsd:integer .

