concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-22 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "22 Engagement of APS employees"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-22 ;
    values:originalText "(1) An Agency Head, on behalf of the Commonwealth, may engage persons as employees for the purposes of the Agency. (2) The engagement of an APS employee (including an engagement under section 72) must be: (a) as an ongoing APS employee; or (b) for a specified term or for the duration of a specified task; or (c) for duties that are irregular or intermittent." ;
    skos:definition "(1) An Agency Head, on behalf of the Commonwealth, may engage persons as employees for the purposes of the Agency. (2) The engagement of an APS employee (including an engagement under section 72) must be: (a) as an ongoing APS employee; or (b) for a specified term or for the duration of a specified task; or (c) for duties that are irregular or intermittent."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "4d1446611631b7401155c71b702ce46a009fb9c64a1cbc6fed0c028f8d8f70f8" ;
    cof:pageNumber "23"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-22-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-22-ss-2 ;
