doc:sec-30-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "30(2) Retirement" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) The minimum retiring age is 55 years, or such higher or lower age as is prescribed by the regulations." ;
    cof:pageNumber "29"^^xsd:integer .

concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-31 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "31 Forfeiture of additional remuneration"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-31 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If an APS employee receives any non-Commonwealth remuneration for performing duties as an APS employee, then the Agency Head may give a notice in writing to the employee in relation to the whole, or a specified part, of the remuneration. (2) The amount notified by the Agency Head: (a) is taken to have been received by the employee on behalf of the Commonwealth; and (b) may be recovered by the Commonwealth from the employee as a debt in a court of competent jurisdiction. (3) If an Agency Head receives any non-Commonwealth remuneration for performing duties as an Agency Head, then the Agency Minister may give a notice in writing to the Agency Head in relation to the whole, or a specified part, of the remuneration. (4) The amount notified by the Agency Minister:" ;
    skos:definition "(1) If an APS employee receives any non-Commonwealth remuneration for performing duties as an APS employee, then the Agency Head may give a notice in writing to the employee in relation to the whole, or a specified part, of the remuneration. (2) The amount notified by the Agency Head: (a) is taken to have been received by the employee on behalf of the Commonwealth; and (b) may be recovered by the Commonwealth from the employee as a debt in a court of competent jurisdiction. (3) If an Agency Head receives any non-Commonwealth remuneration for performing duties as an Agency Head, then the Agency Minister may give a notice in writing to the Agency Head in relation to the whole, or a specified part, of the remuneration. (4) The amount notified by the Agency Minister:"@en ;
