concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-48c a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "48C Termination of appointment"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-48c ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Governor-General may, by notice in writing, on the recommendation of the Prime Minister, terminate the appointment of a Special Commissioner at any time. (2) The Prime Minister must not recommend that the appointment of a Special Commissioner be terminated unless the Prime Minister has consulted the Commissioner about the termination.   The Merit Protection Commissioner  Part 6 Merit Protection Commissioner’s functions etc.  Division 1 Section 49 Public Service Act 1999 Compilation date: 11/12/2024" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Governor-General may, by notice in writing, on the recommendation of the Prime Minister, terminate the appointment of a Special Commissioner at any time. (2) The Prime Minister must not recommend that the appointment of a Special Commissioner be terminated unless the Prime Minister has consulted the Commissioner about the termination.   The Merit Protection Commissioner  Part 6 Merit Protection Commissioner’s functions etc.  Division 1 Section 49 Public Service Act 1999 Compilation date: 11/12/2024"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "edd75f60f953d63791f27c35d03fc960cd21a25e06a1a69af1e8931ddb32ee4e" ;
    cof:pageNumber "52"^^xsd:integer ;
