concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-57 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "57 Roles and responsibilities of Secretaries"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-57 ;
    values:originalText "Roles of Secretaries (1) The roles of the Secretary of a Department include, but are not limited to, the following: (a) principal official policy adviser to the Agency Minister; (b) manager, ensuring delivery of government programs and collaboration to achieve outcomes within the Agency Minister’s portfolio and, with other Secretaries, across the whole of Government; (c) leader, providing stewardship within the Department and, in partnership with the Secretaries Board, across the APS; (d) any other role prescribed by the regulations. Responsibilities of Secretaries (2) The responsibilities of the Secretary of a Department are as follows:" ;
    skos:definition "Roles of Secretaries (1) The roles of the Secretary of a Department include, but are not limited to, the following: (a) principal official policy adviser to the Agency Minister; (b) manager, ensuring delivery of government programs and collaboration to achieve outcomes within the Agency Minister’s portfolio and, with other Secretaries, across the whole of Government; (c) leader, providing stewardship within the Department and, in partnership with the Secretaries Board, across the APS; (d) any other role prescribed by the regulations. Responsibilities of Secretaries (2) The responsibilities of the Secretary of a Department are as follows:"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "da712b4d79ad49f90bd37896a0190ae53632acd2ba41b9012af00937c7fb70c5" ;
    cof:pageNumber "59"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-57-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-57-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <public-service-act-1999.pdf> ;
    dc:source "public-service-act-1999.pdf, p.59" .
