concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-149-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "149 Section 149"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-149-2 ;
    values:originalText "1 of the Criminal Code that relates to this Act). Person not liable to penalty (4) The person is not liable to any penalty under the provisions of any other law by reason of his or her giving the information or producing the document to the Merit Protection Commissioner. Disclosure of personal information is authorised for purposes of Privacy Act (5) To the extent that the giving of the information or the production of the document to the Merit Protection Commissioner involves a disclosure of personal information, the disclosure is taken to be authorised by this Act for the purposes of the Privacy Act 1988. Legal professional privilege not affected (6) Subsection (3) does not otherwise affect a claim of legal professional privilege that anyone may make in relation to the information or document." ;
