concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-73-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "73(5) Payments in special circumstances"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-73-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) Conditions may be attached to payments under this section. If a condition is breached, the payment may be recovered by the Commonwealth as a debt in a court of competent jurisdiction. Note: Payments under this section must be made from money appropriated by the Parliament. Generally, a payment can be debited against an Agency’s annual appropriation, providing that it relates to some matter that has arisen in the course of its administration.   Miscellaneous  Part 11  Section 74 Public Service Act 1999 Compilation date: 11/12/2024" ;
    skos:definition "(5) Conditions may be attached to payments under this section. If a condition is breached, the payment may be recovered by the Commonwealth as a debt in a court of competent jurisdiction. Note: Payments under this section must be made from money appropriated by the Parliament. Generally, a payment can be debited against an Agency’s annual appropriation, providing that it relates to some matter that has arisen in the course of its administration.   Miscellaneous  Part 11  Section 74 Public Service Act 1999 Compilation date: 11/12/2024"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "077dcb7042d8978d9400c6d5f7858fe18fb8acd89d68f0331eb2d3814f34ae4e" ;
    values:partOf concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-73 ;
    cof:pageNumber "82"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Payment recovery upon condition breach" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
